<title>CZECH REPUBLIC: Czech Cokoladovny to pay 70 crown 1996 div.</title>
<headline>Czech Cokoladovny to pay 70 crown 1996 div.</headline>
<dateline>PRAGUE 1997-05-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Czech confectioner Cokoladovny a.s., majority owned by a consortium of Nestle SA and France's Danone, said on Thursday it was proposing to pay out a 70 crown gross dividend per share on 1996 earnings, after 50 crowns in the previous year.</p>
</text>
